.TH OCR-SHOT 1 "August 2026" "ocr-shot 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ocr-shot \- Live Text OCR screenshot utility for Void Linux (Wayland & X11)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocr-shot
[\fILANGUAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-gui\fR] [\fB\-\-cli\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ocr-shot
captures a screen region and interactively extracts text using Tesseract OCR, featuring an Apple Live Text-like visual overlay. Supports multi-language combined scans and dynamic auto-detection of all installed system language packs (Indonesian, English, Arabic, Japanese, Chinese, Korean, Javanese, Sundanese, German, French, Spanish, Russian, etc.).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I LANGUAGE
Target OCR language code(s) separated by '+' (e.g., \fBind+eng+ara\fR, \fBind+eng+ara+jpn+chi_sim\fR, \fBjpn\fR, \fBchi_sim\fR, \fBkor\fR, \fBjav\fR, \fBsun\fR, \fBdeu\fR, \fBfra\fR, \fBspa\fR, \fBrus\fR). Default is \fBind+eng+ara\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Force interactive GUI Live Text overlay mode.
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Force non-interactive CLI mode (copies detected text directly to system clipboard).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Export full text and word bounding box coordinates (x, y, w, h) in structured JSON format.
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDynamic Multi-Language Support\fR: Automatically populates GUI dropdown with all Tesseract language data packs installed on Void Linux.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInteractive Overlay\fR: Screen freeze with word bounding box highlights, click-and-drag text selection, double-click word selection, and triple-click line selection.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSmart Data Detectors\fR: Automatically detects URLs (\fBOpen Link\fR), Email addresses (\fBSend Email\fR), Phone numbers (\fBCall/Copy Phone\fR), and Physical Locations (\fBGoogle Maps\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSelect All Shortcut\fR: Press \fBCtrl+A\fR or click \fBAll\fR to select all detected text instantly.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBContext Menu\fR: Right-click anywhere on selection for quick action context menu.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBParagraph Join Mode\fR: Toggle between raw line breaks and unified paragraph text formatting.
.SH INSTALLING ADDITIONAL LANGUAGES ON VOID LINUX
To install additional language packs for Tesseract on Void Linux, run:
.IP
.B sudo xbps-install -S tesseract-data-<lang>
.PP
Examples:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-jpn\fR (Japanese)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-chi_sim\fR (Chinese Simplified)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-kor\fR (Korean)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-jav\fR (Javanese)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-sun\fR (Sundanese)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-deu\fR (German)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtesseract-data-fra\fR (French)
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/ocr-shot/config.json
Optional user configuration file to customize default settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR xbps-install (1)
